Third-party software
--------------------
concordia is built from open source crates. Every release ships THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, generated by
`cargo about generate about.hbs`, containing each crate's copyright notice and license text.
Dependency licenses are enforced in CI by `cargo deny check` (see deny.toml).

One dependency is not permissively licensed: `option-ext` (pulled in by `dirs`) is MPL-2.0, a
file-level copyleft license. It is used unmodified as a library; its source is available at
https://github.com/soc/option-ext. If it is ever vendored or modified, those files must remain
under MPL-2.0 and be published.
